  "facts": [
    "July 1518, Strasbourg: a woman named Frau Troffea began dancing in the street and kept going for days.",
    "Others joined; within weeks the number of dancers reportedly grew to as many as 400.",
    "Physicians blamed 'hot blood'; the authorities cleared the grain market, built a stage and hired musicians so the dancers could dance it out. It made things worse.",
    "The council then banned public dancing and sent the dancers to a shrine of St. Vitus.",
    "Modern historians (John Waller) explain it as mass psychogenic illness in a city stressed by famine and disease."
